# 1 - Happy path: a claimant files a new claim end to end.
#
# Shows: the claimant describes the incident in plain words, presses "Prepare claim" (one structured-output model
#   call turns the conversation into a validated claim card), confirms it, and the claim is filed in the insurer
#   core with a new claim number. The incident is a harmless class 1 garden event (the "prize rose hedge" claim);
#   it is filed live, so its number is whatever the core hands out next (not 4810, which belongs to script 3).
# Preconditions: stack running (docker compose, auth-server, core-mcp, backend, Ollama) and the desktop started
#   with DESKTOP_CONTROL_PORT=8765.
# Seed: `seed reset` below puts the claims back to the scenario state and deletes every claim filed at runtime.
# Run order: free. Each presentation script stands alone and can run any number of times (usual order 0, 1, 2, 3);
#   3-back-office brings its own claim and does not need this one.
# Pacing: made for unattended runs (`./kaiju demo run`): `pace` is the pause between two actions, `read-pause`
#   the pause after each `wait-idle`, so the audience can read the answer (defaults 1200 ms and 4 s).
#   Step mode (`--step`) is not paced: each `next` runs at once.
# Run: ./kaiju demo run scripts/demos/presentation/1-happy-path.kaiju
#   or step through it: ./kaiju demo start scripts/demos/presentation/1-happy-path.kaiju --step, then ./kaiju demo next
#
# Presenter: the claimant is the fixed demo claimant (customer 1, policy KP-1001), so the filed claim belongs to
#   customer 1. Script 3 reviews the same story as the seeded claim 4810.

seed reset
pace 1200ms
read-pause 5s

persona claimant
new-conversation

send "A class 1 kaiju, a big lizard, ate my prize rose hedge and flattened my garden fence on Hilltop on 18 November at about 4:20 pm. Policy KP-1001. The repair estimate is 120000."
wait-idle 3m
reply

# The claim card appears under the reply.
prepare-claim
wait-idle 3m

# Press Confirm on the card: the claim is filed and the reply names the claim number.
confirm-claim
wait-idle 3m
reply
